cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PETRA in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "PETRA — Prime Exponent Tower Recursive Algebra"
abstract: >
  PETRA is a structural algebra for finite rooted non-plane forms. Its
  intrinsic carrier is defined by finite recursive multisets with primitive
  direct parent-child incidence, intrinsic child multiplicity, no intrinsic
  sibling order, and recursive multiset structural equality. Its executable
  intrinsic core provides ADD and REMOVE structural edits, while the retained
  Leaf/Container/Term/Root model and SPROUT/SHED/GRAFT/PRUNE operators form a
  representation and compatibility layer. Prime and exponent semantics are
  optional derived interpretations rather than prerequisites of the carrier.
type: software
